### Observability endpoints.
### /actuator/prometheus is readable only by the scrape account
### (METRICS_SCRAPE_USERNAME / METRICS_SCRAPE_PASSWORD in .env), never by a
### tenant or platform token. The values below are the .env.example defaults.

### Metrics as the scrape account (expects 200, Prometheus text format)
### Look for jobs_last_success_seconds, notification_outbox_oldest_age_seconds,
### audit_events_total and hikaricp_connections_active.
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/prometheus
Authorization: Basic prometheus dev-only-scrape-password

### Metrics without credentials (expects 401 UNAUTHENTICATED)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/prometheus

### Metrics with the wrong password (expects 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/prometheus
Authorization: Basic prometheus not-the-password

### Auth — log in as acme's seeded admin, for the checks below
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "email": "admin@acme.test",
  "password": "subscriptionhub"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("acmeToken", response.body.token);
%}

### Metrics with a tenant admin's token (expects 401: that chain reads no bearer tokens)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/prometheus
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### Auth — the seeded platform administrator
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "platform@subscriptionhub.test",
  "password": "subscriptionhub"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("platformToken", response.body.token);
%}

### Metrics with a platform token (expects 401: operating the platform is not scraping it)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/prometheus
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### The scrape account on a tenant endpoint (expects 401: Basic exists only on the metrics chain)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Authorization: Basic prometheus dev-only-scrape-password

### Other actuator endpoints as a tenant admin (expects 403: platform infrastructure)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/info
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### Other actuator endpoints as the platform administrator (expects 200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/info
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### Liveness probe (expects 200, public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health/liveness

### Readiness probe (expects 200 once startup, including ApplicationRunners, has finished)
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health/readiness

### A failed login, to watch auth_login_failures_total{principal="tenant"} go up
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "email": "admin@acme.test",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}
